````markdown name=README.md
# ianova-dashboard — Static Tailwind Dashboard (prototype)

A minimal static dashboard scaffold built with Tailwind CSS and Chart.js. Designed as a local/demo-ready version of the ianova dashboard.

Features
- Responsive layout (sidebar + topbar)
- Stat cards, line chart (visitors), bar chart (sales by category)
- Recent activity table
- Mock data included (data/mock-data.json), with inline fallback so the page works without a server

Run locally
1. Recommended: run a local static server (so fetch works)
   - Python 3: `python -m http.server 8000` and open http://localhost:8000
   - Node: `npx http-server` or use VS Code Live Server
2. Or simply open `index.html` directly — script includes an inline fallback mock so charts will render without a server.

Files
- index.html — main page
- assets/js/app.js — chart and UI logic
- data/mock-data.json — sample data (optional; used if fetch succeeds)

Deploy to Vercel
1. Push this project to a GitHub repository.
2. On Vercel, choose "Import Project" and select the repo.
3. There is no build step for this static site — Vercel will auto-deploy the static files. If you want to serve from a specific folder, set the output directory, otherwise leave it blank.
4. Done — your site will be live on a vercel.app domain (optionally add your custom domain).

Next steps I can help with
- Tailor colors/spacing to match your PDF exactly — provide screenshots or details.
- Add more widgets/charts (pie, area, stacked) or table sorting/pagination.
- Replace mock data with a real API and show how to securely fetch data and refresh the charts.
````
